Section: Tweaks
Homepage: https://github.com/ibrahim2100/albrhi-repo
Description: See and skip what plays next, from the Lock Screen.
 .
 ▍WHAT PLAYS NEXT, WITHOUT OPENING THE APP
 A row under the now-playing controls showing the next track — its title, artist and
 cover — on the Lock Screen, in Control Center and in the Dynamic Island. Tap the cover
 to play it now, or skip it without ever opening the app.
 .
 ▍FIVE APPS
 Apple Music, Apple Podcasts, YouTube, YouTube Music and Spotify. Each reads that app's
 own playback queue, so the row shows what the app itself would play next — not a guess.
 .
 ▍SETTINGS IN ALBRHI
 Settings › Albrhi › Albrhi NextUp: a master switch, one per surface — Lock Screen,
 Dynamic Island, Control Center — and one per app. Changes apply immediately, without a
 respring.
 .
 iOS 14.2 through 26. Every hook is chosen at runtime from the iOS version and the host
 process, so one build serves all of them.
 .
 ▍CREDIT — THIS IS A PORT, NOT AN ORIGINAL
 Albrhi NextUp is a port of NextUp 3 by Yves (github.com/Yves000/NextUp3), used and
 redistributed under the GNU GPL v3 — the same licence this project ships under, which
 is what makes carrying the code over lawful where an unlicensed tweak could only be
 read for architecture. The original design, the private-API research and very nearly
 all of the implementation are Yves's work. What this port changes: the Settings pane
 was replaced by a page inside Albrhi Panel, and the package was rebranded. Nothing
 about the feature itself is this project's invention.
 .
 Ported and maintained by Ibrahim Ismail AL-Rahn. Free and open source under the GNU
 GPL v3; the full licence text ships with the source.
