 .
 Albrhi adds a download button to Instagram, clears the clutter out of your feed, and
 lets you watch without the app reporting it. Everything is in one settings panel.
 .
 ▍DOWNLOADS
 A download button in the action row of every post and reel, next to the save icon.
 One tap saves the best quality straight to Photos, or to its own album.
 .
 Stories and view-once messages have their own button. Reels can be saved as video or
 as just the audio. Profile pictures save in full size on a long press.
 .
 ▍DOWNLOAD CENTER
 A proper queue: pause, resume, retry and cancel, several downloads at once, and they
 keep going after you leave the app. Repeated links are spotted, finished files are
 tidied away once they reach Photos, and a searchable history keeps track.
 .
 ▍A QUIETER FEED
 Turn off ads, sponsored posts, suggested posts, suggested accounts, suggested reels,
 Threads posts, Meta AI, the friends map, trending searches and the explore grid.
 Hide the stories tray, or the whole feed.
 .
 ▍PRIVACY
 Watch stories without telling the person who posted it, and choose per story when to
 tell them. View-once photos and videos stay unseen until you tap the eye button on
 that message. Hide the typing indicator and turn off screenshot detection.
 .
 ▍REELS
 Tap to pause or mute instead of liking. Keep the progress bar visible. Stop reels
 unmuting themselves. Hide the header and the blend button.
 .
 ▍CONFIRMATIONS
 An optional "are you sure" before liking, following, reposting, calling, commenting
 or sending a voice message, so a mis-tap does not become a notification.
 .
 ▍ARABIC AND ENGLISH
 Full Arabic and English, with the layout flipping automatically. Choose your own
 accent colour, dark mode included. Open the settings by holding the menu button on
 your profile.
 .
 There is also a diagnostics page. If something does not work, it shows what the tweak
 can actually see on your phone, and sends a report in one tap.
 .
 ▍INSTAGRAM VERSIONS
 Tested on Instagram 410, 439 and 441. Nothing here is tied to a version number — the
 tweak looks for what it needs while the app runs, so other versions should work too.
 .
